Note that on the current version of sisku, however, "do
sisku tu'a la nitcion." works for seeking Nick, because "tu'a" raises to
any abstraction that's needed, not just an event abstraction. However,
"tu'a lo -unicorn" will not work.

Why not? It would be {le ka ce'u du lo pavyseljirna},
just like {le ka ce'u du la nitcion}. The unicorn
case reduces to {le ka ce'u pavyseljirna}, but that
doesn't mean {tu'a lo pavyseljirna} doesn't work.

(The Nick case should reduce to {le ka ce'u nitcion}
if CMENE were BRIVLA, but anyway...)

